    "kind": "certification",
    "proves": "Verify that all expected Globular services are registered in etcd.\n\nExtends the smoke service-health-minimal check to cover the full service\ncatalog: control plane, security, infrastructure, storage, monitoring, and\nAI services. A service present in etcd means it started, connected, and\nannounced its endpoint \u2014 making this a distributed liveness check.\n\nKnown failure modes caught by this test:\n- Service binary crashed before registering (etcd has no entry)\n- systemd dependency ordering failure (service started too early, died)\n- ScyllaDB-dependent services (ai_memory, repository) not registering\n  after ScyllaDB takes time to become ready\n- Workflow service registering with unexpected port (etcd key present\n  but at wrong address)",
